-academy-id "q-72065" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $217$ | $234$ | $268$ | $336$ | $478$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x)-g(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{g(2)-g(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2)-g(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{268-234}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{1} \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72065/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494ef4f7-873c-5d87-85e5-89094c6cc376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72065"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343779/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "0a14edba-101f-5f0f-8493-29f65b5ad90d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343779/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d29b44f2-49df-5106-8c47-3ed86fa2e77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343779/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d17bca4-dfa8-5637-80e2-f68f77f47757" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343779/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-343779/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-343779/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343779" :question/id #uuid "ca6e7459-ab08-5f57-bb26-c78c226031a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343779" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ | $1.1$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $13$ | $15$ | $18$ | $20$ | $22$ | $25$ |\n\nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=1.2$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{f}^{′}(1.2)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=1.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1.2) & ≈\\frac{f(1.2)-f(1.2-0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1.2)-f(1.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{25-22}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{0.1} \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343779/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494ef4f7-873c-5d87-85e5-89094c6cc376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343782/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "0893f434-ab7d-50b6-8c21-5cba86c52d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343782/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5de84170-0bd4-5655-95ef-0e75e8996856" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343782/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer-field/choices ["q-343782/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343782" :question/id #uuid "464a1358-3b78-5c7e-9875-a51dcad5a536" :question/math-academy-id "q-343782" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.75$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $6$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.75$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{f}^{′}(0.75)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=0.75.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.25.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.75) & ≈\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.75-0.25)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.5)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{0.25} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343782/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494ef4f7-873c-5d87-85e5-89094c6cc376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343788/field-1/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" :answer/id #uuid "7b0c0a7d-2feb-5df7-9804-99f3b8902915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343788/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f532fdad-6d44-567e-8e55-a73ddffeee75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343788/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f016f9dc-39b2-573f-b597-bceb05037c3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343788/field-1/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" :answer-field/choices ["q-343788/field-1/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" "q-343788/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343788" :question/id #uuid "12b7a3fa-89bd-53d6-a916-5e09ca0e4446" :question/math-academy-id "q-343788" :question/problem "A distance function $s(t)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.02$ | $0.04$ | $0.06$ | $0.08$ | $0.10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $5$ | $9$ | $13$ | $18$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=0.06$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{s}^{′}(0.06)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t)-s(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=0.06.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.02.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(0.06) & ≈\\frac{s(0.06)-s(0.06-0.02)}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(0.06)-s(0.04)}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.02} \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343788/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494ef4f7-873c-5d87-85e5-89094c6cc376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343788"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72052/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "e56f600e-4430-5dfc-8938-98f4bd31e89b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72052/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "dc1be5b1-ce58-5627-82dd-484adbeab071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72052/selection/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65" :answer/id #uuid "828e1a03-939b-5bf9-bf61-46f9b4788ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72052/selection/ad06fa8bb