 =\\frac{g(2)-g(1)}{1} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection/6021f3fa5edc09898b6674e1a086fe2d8d37ca3917228086cf59acadc0b93e3c" :answer/id #uuid "6d55cd76-bc9d-5826-b06f-a28f74822c22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-22\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection/911fa2d0dc953120cfebd584b593ac0252f2ae134bafbeaaedbed10c56dea335" :answer/id #uuid "c0945dfb-548f-5d3e-97be-6531861e4f98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-31\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection/e77e17ecc3f46ec8130f444ac357c8b4f30e1b7737edaf9605f7afe17e7801a7" :answer/id #uuid "ee4b15de-49cb-5838-92b6-c5fac12decb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection/5eddab8c478a373a43c1f89294f100a7da4847af603a03978651108e9fa8a2c8" :answer/id #uuid "774ce742-db3b-5c08-9889-ce4e5b236c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection/dcb6634fd6fb7e89f5f079b1a636adeeeaeb277c60ce0515b87c10e67ec9d78b" :answer/id #uuid "cd330cec-b2bb-5b88-b0ec-98992ae9c5fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24dca563-27e2-5ebb-9cf9-a88591dea56d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51328/selection/6021f3fa5edc09898b6674e1a086fe2d8d37ca3917228086cf59acadc0b93e3c" :answer-field/choices ["q-51328/selection/6021f3fa5edc09898b6674e1a086fe2d8d37ca3917228086cf59acadc0b93e3c" "q-51328/selection/911fa2d0dc953120cfebd584b593ac0252f2ae134bafbeaaedbed10c56dea335" "q-51328/selection/e77e17ecc3f46ec8130f444ac357c8b4f30e1b7737edaf9605f7afe17e7801a7" "q-51328/selection/5eddab8c478a373a43c1f89294f100a7da4847af603a03978651108e9fa8a2c8" "q-51328/selection/dcb6634fd6fb7e89f5f079b1a636adeeeaeb277c60ce0515b87c10e67ec9d78b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51328" :question/id #uuid "890f170a-8fa1-5f2c-9033-51da6ad42226" :question/math-academy-id "q-51328" :question/problem "The altitude $h(t)$ of a falling object object, measured in meters, is recorded every second for an interval of six seconds. The values of $h(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(t)$ | $200$ | $195$ | $181$ | $159$ | $128$ | $91$ | $51$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the altitude when $t=3$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{h(t)-h(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{h(3)-h(3-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{h(3)-h(2)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{159-181}{1} \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the rate of change of the altitude is $-22\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51328/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6068e54-fa91-5078-86f8-d34f1f1a3ca4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51328"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343833/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a91b1534-01ba-57e1-a8db-7e5965f8b0f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343833/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "104a67c9-2c2b-5ec3-98ec-0cc137041014" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343833/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-343833/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343833" :question/id #uuid "d6b9060a-5e21-57bc-83ba-2a9d11c84c25" :question/math-academy-id "q-343833" :question/problem "The number of deer in a wildlife reserve, measured in hundreds, is given by the function $D(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in years, since the study began. The values of $D(t)$ for several values of $t$ are shown in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $D(t)$ | $5$ | $7$ | $10$ | $14$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the deer population when $t=4$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=4$ is\n{{field-1}} hundreds per year." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{D}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{D(t)-D(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=4.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{D(4)-D(4-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{D(4)-D(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{19-14}{1} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $t=4$ is $5$ hundreds per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343833/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6068e54-fa91-5078-86f8-d34f1f1a3ca4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection/8826c3f1d019e597ff6c8b48e0636dc4a4eef0665cd75b6685e502a9a0e3d6ed" :answer/id #uuid "f5b43a3f-869c-5f52-9480-41cab83bdd71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection/4ac625c3f3e11b082396f7980ec579afb96d079248b8148754054b7987a9d5e3" :answer/id #uuid "05c64f2e-b43a-56a1-90c3-e8efb28e9ebd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.02\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection/8409d3761de75ef3297b853a958dd42111dcd23ad8582933f8067b24b2b89435" :answer/id #uuid "06d4619d-186b-51b7-b887-34a132b4ee51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.05\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection/698bc9b68c1a021aabedd7bfeacb2e40b43f6721565946454b7b64ab83031bd3" :answer/id #uuid "d04b1cb5-e482-52d4-99a5-84068c6245b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.015\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection/73464562c17e8177305edfbe7d204de7aa6963a9b2f4cfa6cf65633c2f0dde5e" :answer/id #uuid "126ab19d-1501-5873-ac93-0ea8ca4db113" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.025\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b11ff88-8211-5080-ace3-99db4ef73418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47485/selection/8826c3f1d019e597ff6c8b48e0636dc4a4eef0665cd75b6685e502a9a0e3d6ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-47485/selection/8826c3f1d019e597ff6c8b48e0636dc4a4eef0665cd75b6685e502a9a0e3d6ed" "q-47485/selection/4ac625c3f3e11b082396f7980ec579afb96d079248b8148754054b7987a9d5e3" "q-47485/selection/8409d3761de75ef3297b853a958dd42111dcd23ad8582933f8067b24b2b89435" "q-47485/selection/698bc9b68c1a021aabedd7bfeacb2e40b43f6721565946454b7b64ab83031bd3" "q-47485/selection/73464562c17e8177305edfbe7d204de7aa6963a9b2f4cfa6cf65633c2f0dde5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47485" :question/id #uuid "c4fbb16c-9818-55d9-b0fe-3dcb50b4a1b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-47485" :question/problem "A baseball is hit by a batter. The distance between the batter and the ball, measured in miles, is given by the function $s(t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $0.015$ | $0.03$ | $0.045$ | $0.05$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ when $t=1$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t)-s(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{s(1)-s(1-0.5)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(1)-s(0.5)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.03-0.015}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.015}{0.5} \\\\  & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is $0.03\\,\\text{mi}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47485/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6068e54-fa91-5078-86f8-d34f1f1a3ca4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection/a5cbb6cb071abfb165afc63a37a053e7a7388ab0919aeefedde895114fccb6be" :answer/id #uuid "6da3c470-8ff4-526b-81e8-19b2d9dd2036" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ liters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection/a5b554f30367d9613e918027327cf0c9a68a480d7e581a48a4c6f7b6f1da951f" :answer/id #uuid "d779623d-6921-5907-a3a1-16f4f70dcf50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ liters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection/380671c4ee2707079901377f7e761ddc83b1469fcf85dc9865bf9ba6447c148c" :answer/id #uuid "e941df27-1d0f-554a-8daf-8c62f00a0b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4$ liters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection/dc5e393a61d487c97faf3ddc3ba3e6b041bbc9069128c94c79fce4655365f5ae" :answer/id #uuid "cd866a51-dfe4-56ca-8bfb-57866c3b9630" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-6$ liters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection/9391f3acd0bf0b2badcf3b2dec5d6c2aaabb41d5bed067ff09cb0d846f3b8a92" :answer/id #uuid "75023b24-2f49-5a3e-8bc6-053d983b628c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ liters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b8d5130-0515-5454-8e63-1391311683e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72075/selection/dc5e393a61d487c97faf3ddc3ba3e6b041bbc9069128c94c79fce4655365f5ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-72075/selection/a5cbb6cb071abfb165afc63a37a053e7a7388ab0919aeefedde895114fccb6be" "q-72075/selection/a5b554f30367d9613e918027327cf0c9a68a480d7e581a48a4c6f7b6f1da951f" "q-72075/selection/380671c4ee2707079901377f7e761ddc83b1469fcf85dc9865bf9ba6447c148c" "q-72075/selection/dc5e393a61d487c97faf3ddc3ba3e6b041bbc9069128c94c79fce4655365f5ae" "q-72075/selection/9391f3acd0bf0b2badcf3b2dec5d6c2aaabb41d5bed067ff09cb0d846f3b8a92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72075" :question/id #uuid "1ae282ea-b8e3-5393-964f-989b3735926f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72075" :question/problem "An oil tank is leaking. The volume of oil in the tank, in liters, after $t$ hours is given by the function $q(t).$ The values of $q(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $q(t)$ | $200$ | $192$ | $186$ | $182$ | $180$ |\n\nApproximate the rate at which the volume of oil in the tank is changing when $t=2$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{q}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{q(t)-q(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{q(2)-q(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =186-192 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of change of the volume is $-6$ liters per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72075/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6068e54-fa91-5078-86f8-d34f1f1a3ca4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343841/field-1/7cafe34cd5fb2a625174720bdef84ba2d3f6ddeb5034bb513dcb1a6b41fce2aa" :answer/id #uuid "8e03e049-5f3e-5ff7-9758-94d9b6aacec1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343841/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bda948df-57d9-507a-bbc7-6c1f9ecc1325" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343841/field-1/7cafe34cd5fb2a625174720bdef84ba2d3f6ddeb5034bb513dcb1a6b41fce2aa" :answer-field/choices ["q-343841/field-1/7cafe34cd5fb2a625174720bdef84ba2d3f6ddeb5034bb513dcb1a6b41fce2aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343841" :question/id #uuid "ab708991-bfbd-575f-9834-64b4bea609d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343841" :question/problem "The battery charge of a delivery drone, measured in percent, is given by the function $B(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the drone was fully charged. The values of $B(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $B(t)$ | $80$ | $72$ | $55$ | $40$ | $35$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the battery charge when $t=6$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=6$ is\n{{field-1}} percent per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{B}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{B(t)-B(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{B(6)-B(6-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{B(6)-B(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-55}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $t=6$ is $-\\frac{15}{2}$ percent per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343841/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6068e54-fa91-5078-86f8-d34f1f1a3ca4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343841"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343858/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "ad5b6392-64ad-55fe-a988-3954b922cc3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343858/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "2b043044-28cc-56a1-aa5c-5e5fbf2fb860" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343858/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc96f7f1-9038-5677-9efd-59393fa9de91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343858/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-343858/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-343858/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343858" :question/id #uuid "f719021c-ba29-5df8-bf19-5b8055797dc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-343858" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/3a4526a6979a86aa924bddca54b05778e91bb67a1dcb6159c5436cc975b22668.png)\n\nA cyclist records the total distance traveled after $x$ minutes. The total distance traveled after $x$ minutes, in miles, is given by the function $D(x).$ The graph of $D(x)$ is shown above.  \n\nApproximate the rate of change when $x=45$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=15.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=30$ and $x=45.$*\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $x=45$ is\n{{field-1}} miles per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{D}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{D(x)-D(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=45.$  Applying the above formula with $x=45$ and $h=15$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(45) & ≈\\frac{D(45)-D(45-15)}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{D(45)-D(30)}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-6}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $x=45$ is $\\frac{1}{3}$ miles per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343858/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d864064-2833-530a-b421-a57f9ec5fce5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection/7567c5e579779f1aa45e31e80998c532598c4cb5db6edeb19a5977996e160b9c" :answer/id #uuid "96f0d52e-57ec-546c-a6ec-c03ec2a4430e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection/883e7137903e1b5ca0caeaddeeda72ab6d31e8ee1bdc57e46ab421be1799461f" :answer/id #uuid "3e4b6dbc-2b9e-5e2f-bee4-437d00075fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "800\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection/19c30ca15588acde6bd6431ecacc3ccf62c13d69cdf2e9a73b42b35e047e67c0" :answer/id #uuid "b44aff20-12b3-5736-a688-3b1c2bd02343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection/5036b5ee1f8f6574d5b9f7a9cbec067b9d53902581d119d89617516295ce96af" :answer/id #uuid "bd2337f3-4b08-5d0e-b98d-65f3d5113587" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "900\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection/10c067fe2f510e300416cc332fddcbae639299f45ebc16f712434f90c8494d96" :answer/id #uuid "e981eeab-d597-50b4-9af0-71828f72945c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "600\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "627ea0c3-c603-50d6-b534-98410e1b7c01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86484/selection/19c30ca15588acde6bd6431ecacc3ccf62c13d69cdf2e9a73b42b35e047e67c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-86484/selection/7567c5e579779f1aa45e31e80998c532598c4cb5db6edeb19a5977996e160b9c" "q-86484/selection/883e7137903e1b5ca0caeaddeeda72ab6d31e8ee1bdc57e46ab421be1799461f" "q-86484/selection/19c30ca15588acde6bd6431ecacc3ccf62c13d69cdf2e9a73b42b35e047e67c0" "q-86484/selection/5036b5ee1f8f6574d5b9f7a9cbec067b9d53902581d119d89617516295ce96af" "q-86484/selection/10c067fe2f510e300416cc332fddcbae639299f45ebc16f712434f90c8494d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86484" :question/id #uuid "0fee9c3a-f0bf-5a94-a09d-085f67b90a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-86484" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/1fcdf0d68d78cba445d1e3ecfeec237ee4e33d7c74cb3b292593fe8b717fe6b8.png)\n\nPeter notices that the total number of eggs produced on his farm $t$ weeks after the beginning of his observations is given by the function $N(t).$ The graph of $N(t)$ is shown above.\n\nApproximate the rate at which the number of produced eggs increases when $t=5$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{N(t)-N(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=5.$ Applying the above formula with $t=5$ and $h=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{N(5)-N(5-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{N(5)-N(4)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{800-600}{1} \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of increase is $200\\,\\text{eggs}/\\text{week}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86484/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d864064-2833-530a-b421-a57f9ec5fce5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86484"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343862/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "62094e1b-52dd-594e-aa6a-251ca1d942e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343862/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "df9ac778-ac39-513d-95b0-966ef7c0c963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343862/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8304bd21-4ab9-51f9-bcd9-dee51fb9070a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343862/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-343862/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-343862/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343862" :question/id #uuid "d0b47029-aa71-51b9-a42b-48c9fb06a339" :question/math-academy-id "q-343862" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/9a5fa5cdd4734813d18af5b99e3869051f15e137f72e98ad5529c751e6f85d87.png)\n\nA model rocket’s height is recorded during a launch. The height after $x$ seconds, in meters, is given by the function $H(x).$ The graph of $H(x)$ is shown above.  \n\nApproximate the rate of change when $x=16$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=12.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=4$ and $x=16.$*\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $x=16$ is\n{{field-1}} meters per second." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{H}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{H(x)-H(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=16.$  Applying the above formula with $x=16$ and $h=12$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{′}(16) & ≈\\frac{H(16)-H(16-12)}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(16)-H(4)}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-5}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $x=16$ is $\\frac{1}{6}$ meters per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343862/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d864064-2833-530a-b421-a57f9ec5fce5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection/2275cf3763e314d03fd58482ce8504a6e36adbad2ee08fc1d30138f2587b6f77" :answer/id #uuid "f35d6dfd-1f7f-5da5-9f12-f9d159915369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{liters}/\\text{hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection/4c8f022b7e889ba85fd795977a3ab9202340d36fb8ba19ad6403a5d48783e5f3" :answer/id #uuid "bbb73932-a3f6-5f04-840f-519101f3fb93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{liter}/\\text{hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection/1c46971ddd72d9e5d3654c85ef1850a8daea3d48f172560bf1343ad32a3c8bb1" :answer/id #uuid "d9a6c514-0b33-583a-a334-181957f98242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5\\,\\text{liters}/\\text{hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection/a5c15092b247ca952a7739a4e4db60e5bc28018e7b737be4b1ac47f9452a3cdd" :answer/id #uuid "5d9ffc89-40d3-5fa3-8283-cf4e49db918a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{liters}/\\text{hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection/a4bfc02608c132de4480bf60834fce0619836bad593ac6115702e2fe1145d942" :answer/id #uuid "394e5480-69da-5762-987b-e2fa2fa71b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{liters}/\\text{hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a15028-c5cb-55d5-88d6-5f1818ed5cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47357/selection/a4bfc02608c132de4480bf60834fce0619836bad593ac6115702e2fe1145d942" :answer-field/choices ["q-47357/selection/2275cf3763e314d03fd58482ce8504a6e36adbad2ee08fc1d30138f2587b6f77" "q-47357/selection/4c8f022b7e889ba85fd795977a3ab9202340d36fb8ba19ad6403a5d48783e5f3" "q-47357/selection/1c46971ddd72d9e5d3654c85ef1850a8daea3d48f172560bf1343ad32a3c8bb1" "q-47357/selection/a5c15092b247ca952a7739a4e4db60e5bc28018e7b737be4b1ac47f9452a3cdd" "q-47357/selection/a4bfc02608c132de4480bf60834fce0619836bad593ac6115702e2fe1145d942"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47357" :question/id #uuid "356c9356-b943-5cfb-849c-968981b6e053" :question/math-academy-id "q-47357" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/64e35c559b233a28c5913ffa37ad949653ad2b46a0e10db639626b8575b7a263.png)\n\nAn oil tank is leaking $q(t)$ liters of oil, where $t>0$ is the time in hours since the leak started.\n The graph of $q(t)$ is shown above.\n\nApproximate the rate at which the oil is leaking from the tank when $t=2$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{q}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{q(t)-q(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=2.$ Applying the above formula with $t=2$ and $h=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{q(2)-q(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-1}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the rate of leaking is $2\\,\\text{liters}/\\text{hour}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d864064-2833-530a-b421-a57f9ec5fce5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343869/field-1/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d" :answer/id #uuid "fa295e88-7dd7-548a-8b7f-d90bc23f98b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343869/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ba6acf-8fbb-5bb3-8957-0d010726cc04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343869/field-1/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d" :answer-field/choices ["q-343869/field-1/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343869" :question/id #uuid "771ddffa-f1c8-5e73-8081-54fdf5cab8e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-343869" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/fd917228308b839be77110b07e32fa0154350c290920628400bd1f20a34160b5.png)\n\nA factory tracks the number of defective items remaining after a recall. The number of defective items after $x$ days, in hundreds, is given by the function $N(x).$ The graph of $N(x)$ is shown above.  \n\nApproximate the rate of change when $x=15$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=10$ and $x=15.$*\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $x=15$ is\n{{field-1}} hundred items per day." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{N(x)-N(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=15.$  Applying the above formula with $x=15$ and $h=5$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}^{′}(15) & ≈\\frac{N(15)-N(15-5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{N(15)-N(10)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{72-76}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the estimated rate of change when $x=15$ is $-\\frac{4}{5}$ hundred items per day." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343869/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d864064-2833-530a-b421-a57f9ec5fce5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343869"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-155"] :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ | $7$ | $10$ | $13$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-12$ | $-7$ | $-3$ | $7$ | $15$ | $21$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=16$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x) - f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=16.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(16) & ≈\\frac{f(16)-f(16-3)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(16)-f(13)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{21-15}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6104"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/6e3f77e5b7d491e3ee43c8f8150065282d2abc259e3a88751b93ff15b27f492a.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=6$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\frac{g(x) - g(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=6.$ Applying the above formula with $x=6$ and $h=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{g(6)-g(6-4)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-156"] :question/problem "A race car's position along a straight track, measured in meters from the starting line, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ | $2.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $1.3$ | $2.7$ | $2.9$ | $3.5$ | $5.0$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s'(t)$ when $t=1.6$ using a backward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\ns'(t) \\approx \\frac{s(t) - s(t-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=1.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(1.6) & ≈\\frac{s(1.6)-s(1.6-0.2)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(1.6)-s(1.4)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.9-2.7}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at the time $t=1.6,$ the velocity is approximately $1\\, \\textrm{m}/\\textrm{s}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6105"] :question/problem "A factory produces fans. The total cost of producing $x$ fans, in dollars, is given by the function $C(x).$  The graph of $C(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/ad3fae3694c4df8269be9a54350aabf83368b3152ea69eb2b9d1ac76e702823f.png)\n\nApproximate the marginal cost $C'(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\nC'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{C(x) - C(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3.$ Applying the above formula with $x=3$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{C(3)-C(3-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{C(3)-C(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-20}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the marginal cost is $\\[math]5$ per fan." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
